UID:10012230-1791637200-1791646200@njaudubon.org
SUMMARY:NJ Audubon: Digital Photography Workshop: Photography Boot Camp
DESCRIPTION:Instructors: David DesRochers\, Phil Witt\, Jack Moskowitz\, NJ Audubon Associate Naturalists. \nParticipants will apply what they learned in Understanding Your Camera Workshop. This will be a hands-on session with cameras\, with participants practicing changing camera settings\, compensation for varying light conditions. We will practice composition using set ups\, considering the effect of light quality and direction\, distance to subject\, focal length\, and f/stop. \nRegistration required at Eventbrite by 10/09 at 4:00 PM. \n\n\n\n\nCOST: $18 members\, $30 nonmembers. \n\n\n\n\n\nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \n\n\nCANCELLATION: NJ Audubon’s programs require a minimum number of registrants to run. If we cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, all participants will be notified as soon as possible and are eligible for a full refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 48 hours in advance. Sorry\, no refund for cancellations less than 48 hours in advance unless due to health emergencies; however\, registrations can be transferred to another program in the future. \n\n\nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/nj-audubon-digital-photography-workshop-photography-boot-camp-2/
LOCATION:New Jersey Audubon’s Scherman Hoffman Wildlife Sanctuary\, 11 Hardscrabble Road\, Bernardsville\, NJ\, 07924\, United States
CATEGORIES:Scherman Hoffman Wildlife Sanctuary,Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Digital-Photography-Workshop-Understanding-your-camera.jpg
GEO:40.7448693;-74.5523161
