SUMMARY:Seabird ID Mini-Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The migration of scoters and other sea ducks\, loons\, cormorants and gannets can be an overwhelming sight.  For example\, the CMBO full-time Avalon Seawatch project sighted over one million seabirds here in 2014! Join CMBO interpretive naturalists for this outdoor workshop to witness and learn about this migration spectacle.  Meets at the Avalon Seawatch location on the Beach between 8th and 9th St.\, at the north end of Avalon. NO preregistration required.  \nIMPORTANT INFORMATION:  \n\nBring binoculars\, scope and tripod\, if available\nDress in layers for wind\, cold\, or warm weather\n\nCOST: FREE \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/seabird-id-mini-workshop-8/2026-10-10/
LOCATION:Avalon Seawatch\, Avalon\, NJ\, 08202\, United States
CATEGORIES:Birding,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/Seabird-ID-mini-Workshop_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:39.107686162731;-74.705991666639
END:VEVENT
